WEBVTT

Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
<v Narrator> 1: Introduction

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Hey! Welcome to Loki's Lab. I'm here to show you how to run the V3 test harness

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
— it's a simple way to benchmark your local AI model and see how it stacks up on

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
the leaderboard.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000


00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The whole process takes just a few minutes to set up, and then you kick off the

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
tests and grab a coffee while they run. Let's get started!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.000
<v Narrator> 2: What You Need

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.529
Here's what you'll need:

00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:37.058


00:00:37.058 --> 00:00:40.588
First, a machine with at least 16 gigabytes of RAM. The bigger models we test

00:00:40.588 --> 00:00:44.117
need a little breathing room, so 16 is the minimum, but 32 or more is even

00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:47.647
better.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:51.176


00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:54.705
Second, Ollama — that's the app that runs local AI models. It's totally free and

00:00:54.705 --> 00:00:58.235
works on Mac, Linux, and Windows with WSL2.

00:00:58.235 --> 00:01:01.764


00:01:01.764 --> 00:01:05.294
You'll also need Python 3.8 or newer — most of you probably already have this,

00:01:05.294 --> 00:01:08.823
but we'll show you how to check.

00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:12.352


00:01:12.352 --> 00:01:15.882
And finally, about 50 gigabytes of free disk space. That's mostly for the model

00:01:15.882 --> 00:01:19.411
itself, which is around 22 gigs.

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:22.941


00:01:22.941 --> 00:01:26.470
If you're not sure about any of this, don't worry — the how-to guide has

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:30.000
step-by-step instructions for everything.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.000
<v Narrator> 3: Install Ollama

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.500
Let's start by installing Ollama. Head over to ollama.ai and click the Download

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:45.000
button.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.500


00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:00.000
Pick your operating system — we've got macOS, Linux, and Windows with WSL2.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.500


00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Download the installer, double-click it, and let it do its thing. On Mac, you'll

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.500
drag Ollama into your Applications folder. On Linux, it's a one-command install.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:30.000


00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Give it a minute to finish, and then launch Ollama. You'll see it pop up in your

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:45.000
menu bar on Mac, or as a background service on Linux.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:52.500


00:02:52.500 --> 00:03:00.000
That's it! Ollama is now running and ready to download models.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.000
<v Narrator> 4: Download the Test Harness

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Alright, now let's get the test harness. Open up your Terminal — that's the

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.000
command-line app on your machine.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000


00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.000
First, we'll create a folder to work in. Type this:

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.000


00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.000
mkdir -p ~/loki-v3-test

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.000


00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Then change into that folder:

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.000


00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.000
cd ~/loki-v3-test

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000


00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Now, download the test harness:

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000


00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.000
curl -fsSL https://lokislab.org/eval/v3_test_harness.sh -o v3_test_harness.sh

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.000


00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.000
And make it executable:

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.000


00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.000
chmod +x v3_test_harness.sh

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000


00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Done! You now have the test harness ready to go.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.000
<v Narrator> 5: Pre-Cache the Model

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Before we run the tests, let's pre-download the model. This usually takes 10 to

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.000
30 minutes on first run, depending on your internet speed.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:15.000


00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:20.000
In the same Terminal, type:

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:25.000


00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:30.000
ollama pull qwen3.6:latest

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.000


00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.000
You'll see a progress bar as it downloads the 22-gigabyte model. Go grab a

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.000
coffee, check your email — whatever you need to do while this downloads.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.000


00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.000
If your download is slow, the how-to guide has some tips for troubleshooting.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:00.000
But for most people, this just works.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.000
<v Narrator> 6: Run the Tests

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:07.058
Once the model finishes downloading, you're ready to run the tests. Just type:

00:05:07.058 --> 00:05:14.117


00:05:14.117 --> 00:05:21.176
./v3_test_harness.sh

00:05:21.176 --> 00:05:28.235


00:05:28.235 --> 00:05:35.294
And hit Enter. The script will do a quick check to make sure everything is set

00:05:35.294 --> 00:05:42.352
up correctly, then start running through the 18 tests.

00:05:42.352 --> 00:05:49.411


00:05:49.411 --> 00:05:56.470
You'll see output like this as each test completes — it shows the test name, how

00:05:56.470 --> 00:06:03.529
long it took, and quality scores from 1 to 5.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:10.588


00:06:10.588 --> 00:06:17.647
These tests cover everything: web design, writing, graphics, coding, math,

00:06:17.647 --> 00:06:24.705
vision, and more. Each one usually takes 30 seconds to a few minutes depending

00:06:24.705 --> 00:06:31.764
on your hardware.

00:06:31.764 --> 00:06:38.823


00:06:38.823 --> 00:06:45.882
The whole suite typically takes 2 to 4 hours. So yeah, this is a good time to

00:06:45.882 --> 00:06:52.941
take a break! The tests run in the background, so you can close your Terminal

00:06:52.941 --> 00:07:00.000
and come back later.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.000
<v Narrator> 7: Check Your Results

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.454
When the tests finish, all your results get saved to a results folder. You can

00:07:05.454 --> 00:07:10.909
check them anytime by typing:

00:07:10.909 --> 00:07:16.363


00:07:16.363 --> 00:07:21.818
ls -la results/

00:07:21.818 --> 00:07:27.272


00:07:27.272 --> 00:07:32.727
Each test gets its own JSON file with all the details — whether it passed, the

00:07:32.727 --> 00:07:38.181
quality score, how fast it ran, and the model's actual response.

00:07:38.181 --> 00:07:43.636


00:07:43.636 --> 00:07:49.090
You can peek at any result file to see exactly what your model did. But you

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:54.545
don't need to understand the JSON — that's just so we can aggregate everything

00:07:54.545 --> 00:08:00.000
for the leaderboard.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.000
<v Narrator> 8: Submit Your Results

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.285
Now for the fun part: submitting your results to the Loki's Lab leaderboard!

00:08:04.285 --> 00:08:08.571


00:08:08.571 --> 00:08:12.857
Head over to lokislab.org/test/results. You'll see other people's results,

00:08:12.857 --> 00:08:17.142
ranked by hardware and model.

00:08:17.142 --> 00:08:21.428


00:08:21.428 --> 00:08:25.714
Click the 'Submit a benchmark result' button, upload your JSON files, and boom —

00:08:25.714 --> 00:08:30.000
your machine is on the leaderboard!

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.285


00:08:34.285 --> 00:08:38.571
You can see how your hardware compares to others. Did your MacBook M1 beat a

00:08:38.571 --> 00:08:42.857
fancy Linux box? Did that old laptop surprise everyone? The leaderboard shows it

00:08:42.857 --> 00:08:47.142
all.

00:08:47.142 --> 00:08:51.428


00:08:51.428 --> 00:08:55.714
Your results are public, but completely anonymous unless you add your name. So

00:08:55.714 --> 00:09:00.000
submit with confidence!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.000
<v Narrator> 9: Outro

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.333
That's it! You've just benchmarked your local AI model and joined the Loki's Lab

00:09:03.333 --> 00:09:06.666
community.

00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:10.000


00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.333
If you run into any issues, the full how-to guide is at

00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:16.666
lokislab.org/docs/V3-TEST-HOWTO.md — it's got detailed troubleshooting for

00:09:16.666 --> 00:09:20.000
everything.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.333


00:09:23.333 --> 00:09:26.666
Thanks for testing with us, and we can't wait to see what your machine can do.

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:30.000
Happy benchmarking!
